    scenario:
      'Your meal-kit support agent has three subscription tools: `skip_delivery` for one upcoming box, `pause_subscription` for one to eight weeks, and `cancel_subscription` to end the plan. Last month their descriptions were rewritten with input formats, example requests and when-to-use-which boundaries. In an offline test of the tools on their own, without the production system prompt, 97% of 300 real messages now route correctly. In production, 22% of messages like "cancel next week\'s box, I\'m away" still reach `cancel_subscription`. The system prompt, unchanged since the pilot, says: "If a customer mentions cancelling, start the cancellation flow with `cancel_subscription` and offer the 20% save discount."',
